    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d325-a6">

                <pb facs="0454" n="374" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg374"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 5.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Chapman, agent for steamer Mainlander, to Mr.
                        Lavin, immigrant inspector.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Seattle, Wash.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-06-28"><hi rendition="#italic">June 28,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: Regarding the care of the nine
                    Japanese that arrived on the steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Mainlander</hi>
                    from Vancouver, British Columbia, would state:</p>
                <p>After consultation with Colonel Fisher, it was thought advisable to take them to
                    the county jail for safe-keeping, as well as for their own comfort, there being
                    no suitable place on the dock for them, as the weather was very cool.</p>
                <p>We paid all bills for their care at the jail March 8, 1901.</p>
                <p>Yours, very truly,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. P. Chapman</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Agent Steamer Mainlander.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
